{
    "id": 219,
    "title": "Send to Maps: a journey's whole route to Google Maps or Apple Maps, every stop, in legs when long",
    "why": "decisions/0174 release 1 (accepted 2026-11-19). The route icon on a suggested journey and a place's 'Make a day of it' opened Google Maps only and cut every stop after the tenth without a word. Send to Maps lets a visitor pick Google Maps or Apple Maps and start from their location or the first stop (both remembered on the device), and sends every stop in order, in legs ('Leg 1 of 2') when one link can't hold them. It's a plain link: no key, no call from our server, no cost. Also fixed, the same rules as Directions: a shelter or a mailbox could appear as a stop in a suggested journey, and a private place as a landmark's place to eat.",
